(ned -- helper for cal_a_zero. ONE SUB PER FILE: LinuxCNC resolves)
(subroutines through SUBROUTINE_PATH, and a second sub defined in)
(the calling file is NOT found -- "EOF in file ... seeking o-word",)
(reproduced offline with rs274. Shared setup arrives in GLOBAL)
(parameters; the result goes back the same way.)
(======================== helper: ONE wall touch ===========================)
(#1 = plunge depth below the puck top. Returns #<_ca_ty>.)
o<ca_touch> sub
  #<dep> = #1

  (hover, then out to the standoff OUTSIDE the puck)
  G90
  G1 Z[#<_ca_top> + #<_ca_safe>] F[#<_ca_ftr>]
  G1 X#<_ca_cx> Y[#<_ca_cy> + #<_ca_side> * #<_ca_stand>] F[#<_ca_ftr>]

  (protective descent: if this TRIPS, the standoff is still over the puck --)
  (the puck is wider than the standoff. Never plunge blind.)
  G91
  G38.3 Z-[#<_ca_safe> + #<dep>] F[#<_ca_fck>]
  o105 if [#5070 EQ 1]
    G90
    G1 Z[#<_ca_top> + #<_ca_safe>] F[#<_ca_ftr>]
    M65 P3
    M50 P1
    (abort, CAL A: contact while descending at the standoff - the puck is wider than the 30 mm standoff. Increase _ca_stand.)
  o105 endif

  (probe INWARD toward the axis; the wall stops us)
  G38.3 Y[0 - #<_ca_side> * #<_ca_reach>] F[#<_ca_fpr>]
  o110 if [#5070 EQ 0]
    G90
    G1 Z[#<_ca_top> + #<_ca_safe>] F[#<_ca_ftr>]
    M65 P3
    M50 P1
    (abort, CAL A: NO WALL at this depth. The puck body must extend this far down and share its diameter - reduce the deep plunge or tell me the real geometry.)
  o110 endif
  G1 Y[#<_ca_side> * #<_ca_back>] F[#<_ca_ftr>]
  G38.2 Y[0 - #<_ca_side> * [#<_ca_back> + 1]] F[#<_ca_fla>]
  #<_ca_ty> = #5062

  (clear the wall, back to hover)
  G1 Y[#<_ca_side> * 2] F[#<_ca_ftr>]
  G90
  G1 Z[#<_ca_top> + #<_ca_safe>] F[#<_ca_ftr>]
o<ca_touch> endsub

M2 (end helper)
